{"id":236576572271139,"type":"album","name":"Contra","artist":"Vampire Weekend","year":2010,"weight":19,"info":{"cover":"https://dn711008.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-936707a6-3095-38cb-9261-329e0e246fd4/mbid-936707a6-3095-38cb-9261-329e0e246fd4-28637558356.jpg","yt":"mGu0IYyncZ4","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/vampire-weekend/contra"},"desc":"Contra is the second album by American indie rock band Vampire Weekend, released in January 2010 on XL Recordings. It debuted at number one on the Billboard 200. The album title is intended as a thematic allegory and a complex reference to the Nicaraguan counter-revolutionaries, the 1980 The Clash album Sandinista!, and partially to the Contra video game. Music and lyrics The lyrics of \"I Think Ur a Contra\" include the phrase \"Complete Control\", the title of a Clash single (notably, an influential 1980 triple album by The Clash was entitled Sandinista! after the socialist militancy opposed by the Contras ."},"artist_ref":{"id":195066070988046,"name":"Vampire Weekend","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Vampire_Weekend_Red_Rocks_05.20.13.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":210192360016800,"type":"genre","name":"Alternative Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":2664,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":8412226417108,"type":"genre","name":"Indie Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1139,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":135494496540693,"type":"genre","name":"Indie Pop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":340,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":126030611694007,"type":"genre","name":"Art Pop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":310,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":221854534300578,"type":"genre","name":"Afrobeat","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":224,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":121802802114504,"type":"genre","name":"worldbeat","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":3,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":55143051280122,"type":"genre","name":"Indietronica",